<figure id="S3.F5.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;"><img src="2509.15185v1/exp_attn.png" id="S3.F5.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/121;" width="476" height="121" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="S3.F5.fig2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attention maps of LlamaGen-B model trained with our ST-AR method.</span> We utilize features from the final transformer layer, selecting random steps to draw attention maps. These maps exhibit an expanded effective receptive field, moving beyond mere focus on spatially adjacent and conditional tokens, and reveal distinct semantic patterns.</figcaption>
</figure>
          
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model comparisons on <span id="S3.T2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ImageNet</span>-<math id="S3.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math> Benchmark.</span> All the results are evaluated with CFG. †means the model is trained on <math id="S3.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="384\times 384" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>384</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>384</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">384\times 384</annotation></semantics></math> resolution and resized to <math id="S3.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math> resolution for evaluation. ST-AR consistently beats baseline LlamaGen on all model sizes and training costs.</figcaption>
