<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset.</span>
We evaluate the effectiveness of ST-AR on the class-conditional image generation task using the widely adopted ImageNet-<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math> dataset.
We employ the same VQGAN<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> as LlamaGen<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> for tokenization, precomputing the image token sequences before training.
Following LlamaGen, we also compute tokens for ten crops of the original image.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation metrics.</span>
Since our ST-AR generative model is trained with self-supervised losses to enhance its visual modeling capabilities, we holistically evaluate ST-AR on image understanding and generation.
For image understanding, we use the top-<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy of linear probing as the primary metric.
We adopt the linear probing setup of MAE<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>, training a linear layer for <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>90</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90</annotation></semantics></math> epochs using the representations from the sixth layer.
For image generation, we use the ADM evaluation suite and report Fréchet Inception Distance (FID)<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> as the main evaluation metric.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training &amp; Inference.</span>
All the models are trained with the same setting as LlamaGen: base learning rate of <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> per <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256</annotation></semantics></math> batch size, AdamW optimizer with <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9,\beta_{2}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9,\beta_{2}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay set to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math> and gradient clipping set to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. We train our models on images with <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math> resolution, rather than LlamaGen with <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="384\times 384" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>384</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>384</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">384\times 384</annotation></semantics></math> training images. The teacher model is updated through the exponential moving average of the student model with an EMA decay of <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9999</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9999</annotation></semantics></math>.
The class token embedding dropout ratio is <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> for classifier-free guidance.
The contrastive loss is added on the medium of the transformer network, <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span> the <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\text{-}th" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\text{-}th</annotation></semantics></math> layer for LlamaGen-B, <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="18\text{-}th" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">18\text{-}th</annotation></semantics></math> layer for LlamaGen-L and <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="18\text{-}th" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">18\text{-}th</annotation></semantics></math> layer for LlamaGen-XL.
The masking ratio used for mask image modeling in Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 3.3.1 Masked Learning for Longer Contexts ‣ 3.3 Self-Guided Training for Autoregressive Models ‣ 3 Method ‣ Understand Before You Generate: Self-Guided Training for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is set to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0.25</annotation></semantics></math>.
The number of steps used in Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 3.3.2 Contrastive Learning for Consistency ‣ 3.3 Self-Guided Training for Autoregressive Models ‣ 3 Method ‣ Understand Before You Generate: Self-Guided Training for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ 3.3.2 Contrastive Learning for Consistency ‣ 3.3 Self-Guided Training for Autoregressive Models ‣ 3 Method ‣ Understand Before You Generate: Self-Guided Training for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> is set as <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=4</annotation></semantics></math>.
The weights of reconstruction loss and contrastive loss in Eq. <a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ 3.3.3 Training Losses. ‣ 3.3 Self-Guided Training for Autoregressive Models ‣ 3 Method ‣ Understand Before You Generate: Self-Guided Training for Autoregressive Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> are set to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> by default. For inference, we use the same sampling strategy as LlamaGen.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span><span id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The effects of proposed losses.</span> ST-AR improves linear probing and generation quality.</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T3.4" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_pruned_first">
          
